{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-04 architecture RESEARCH critique recorded at `.joe-janitor/rp04-adr-research-critique.md`; Gitleaks scanned the recovery archive afterward and found no leaks. ADR DRAFT remains blocked pending maintainer response and one bounded research closure.\n\n1. Assumptions: the target whole-application snapshot invariant is not yet an implementation proof; subprocess filtering protects only exact Rebar-declared names and is not a sandbox; Pydantic secret wrappers are defense in depth; native pre-client seams are verified only for researched current providers. These become explicit claims/verification limits.\n2. Uninvestigated dependency: the provider matrix omitted application-owned/observability secret consumers—Langfuse OTLP credentials, local/opcert signing keys, opcert guard, MCP static/introspection/proxy secrets, and review-bot Gerrit/webhook tokens. Before ADR prose, perform a bounded source/ADR census and classify each as provider-owned, deployment-owned static adapter input, or Rebar-owned security material. Future GitHub/GitLab/Jenkins adapters remain non-normative examples.\n3. Proposed resolutions: one atomic ADR about the application composition boundary; CLI creates one operation snapshot (no redundant long-lived bootstrap snapshot); services own startup policy/runtime bindings and create per-operation non-secret snapshots; each adapter declares exact secret env names and a shared child-env builder inherits ambient, removes unrelated declared names, overlays only owning-child material, and never mutates global os.environ; identity checks are conditional on configured expectations and safe SDK metadata; no initial keyring/file-watcher/cloud-secret broker.\n4. Existing constraints: use project-native numbered `docs/adr/`, generated marker/index, lowercase `docs/architecture.md`, and Gerrit—not the generic skill’s `docs/decisions`/GitHub path. Relate/amend ADR 0008 rotation visibility; preserve ADRs 0014/0050 auth semantics; supplement ADR 0041 sanitization under ADR 0046 bounded claims; refine rather than replace ADRs 0059/0083; keep stdlib core rather than adopt pydantic-settings.\n\nProposed next step after maintainer acceptance: close the bounded non-provider secret census, then enter ADR DRAFT. No ADR prose, epic, stories, or production code created yet."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786940079039907001,"uuid":"1488fbcd-3e21-4868-b5f3-74effd5cbb7f"}